{#
  T-8.15 — the merchant's discount popup.

  ⚠ THIS IS NOT `salla-offer-modal`, WHICH `master.twig` ALSO RENDERS. That is
  the platform's **bank-offer** dialog, built from store data, with no merchant
  copy and no coupon of its own. Neither replaces the other, and the two must not
  be confused when reading this layout.

  IT IS T-2.10'S SHEET, NOT A SECOND OVERLAY. Focus in, focus trapped, focus
  returned to whatever had it, `Esc`, backdrop click, the scroll lock and the
  centred shape above tablet are all the primitive's — and the primitive gets
  them from `<dialog>` + `showModal()`. This file supplies a body and a class.
  A second overlay implementation would be a defect, not an alternative.

  `variant: 'dialog'` AND NOT `'sheet'`, WHICH IS A DELIBERATE CHOICE. A bottom
  sheet is the answer to a control the visitor pressed at the bottom of the
  screen — the sign-in button, a card's quick view. **This overlay interrupts
  rather than responds**; nothing was pressed, so a shape that rises from the
  thumb implies a gesture nobody made. No artboard rules on it; recorded in
  /docs/DERIVED-DECISIONS.md.

  ⚠ NO TITLE MEANS NO POPUP, AND THAT IS AN ACCESSIBILITY RULE RATHER THAN AN
  EDITORIAL ONE. T-2.10 uses the title as the dialog's accessible name, and an
  untitled dialog is announced as just «مربّع حوار». **No default copy was
  invented to paper over it**: the artboards' Arabic is illustrative, and a
  made-up heading in the manifest would put words nobody wrote into a live store.
  The setting's own description says so, in the panel, where the merchant is.

  THE IMAGE IS DECORATIVE, ON PURPOSE AND WITH NO `alt` FIELD. The offer is the
  title and the body; the picture repeats it. Adding an `alt` setting would ask
  the merchant to describe a decoration, and the usual result is the file name
  read aloud before the actual message. `alt=""` keeps the announcement clean.

  THE CODE IS WRAPPED IN `<bdi>`. A Latin coupon inside an Arabic sentence
  otherwise reorders around the neighbouring punctuation — the same reason the
  video carousel wraps its poster name.
#}
{% set discount_popup_title = theme.settings.get('discount_popup_title') %}
{% set discount_popup_text = theme.settings.get('discount_popup_text') %}
{% set discount_popup_code = theme.settings.get('discount_popup_code') %}
{% set discount_popup_image = theme.settings.get('discount_popup_image') %}

{% if theme.settings.get('discount_popup_enabled', false) and discount_popup_title %}
    {% set discount_popup_body %}
        <div class="discount-popup">
            {% if discount_popup_image %}
                {#
                  The box is reserved by `.discount-popup__media`'s aspect-ratio
                  rather than by attributes: a merchant's upload has dimensions no
                  template can know, and inventing a pair would squash it. This is
                  the same mechanism every media well in this theme uses.
                #}
                <div class="discount-popup__media">
                    <img class="discount-popup__image"
                         src="{{ discount_popup_image }}"
                         alt=""
                         loading="lazy"
                         decoding="async">
                </div>
            {% endif %}

            {% if discount_popup_text %}
                <p class="discount-popup__text">{{ discount_popup_text }}</p>
            {% endif %}

            {% if discount_popup_code %}
                <div class="discount-popup__code-row">
                    <p class="discount-popup__code" data-discount-code>
                        <bdi>{{ discount_popup_code }}</bdi>
                    </p>

                    {#
                      One control, and it is a real `<button>` — the copy is a
                      side effect on this page, not a navigation. `data-code`
                      carries the value so the script never has to read text back
                      out of the DOM and inherit whatever whitespace the template
                      put there.
                    #}
                    {#
                      NO ICON, AND THAT IS THE CAREFUL ANSWER RATHER THAN A
                      MINIMAL ONE. `sallaicons` ships no `copy` glyph — the font
                      was read on 2026-08-13, not recalled — and the nearest
                      candidates (`pages`, `clipboard-person`) are names whose
                      *appearance* could not be verified from this repository.
                      The button carries a visible label, so an icon here would be
                      decoration bought at the price of a guess.
                    #}
                    <button type="button"
                            class="btn btn--primary discount-popup__copy"
                            data-discount-copy
                            data-code="{{ discount_popup_code }}">
                        <span data-discount-copy-label>{{ trans('theme.discount.copy') }}</span>
                    </button>
                </div>

                {#
                  ⚠ THE CONFIRMATION LIVES HERE, INSIDE THE DIALOG, AND A TOAST
                  WOULD HAVE BEEN THE OBVIOUS WRONG ANSWER. `salla.notify` is what
                  T-7.08 uses for the wishlist, and it renders into `<body>` — but
                  a dialog opened with `showModal()` is in the browser's TOP
                  LAYER, so the toast would paint behind this panel on every
                  store, invisibly. A live region in the dialog's own body is both
                  seen and announced.

                  `polite` and not `assertive`: the visitor pressed the button, so
                  they are already looking at it.
                #}
                <p class="discount-popup__status"
                   data-discount-status
                   role="status"
                   aria-live="polite"></p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    {% endset %}

    {% include 'components.ui.bottom-sheet' with {
        id:      'discount-popup',
        variant: 'dialog',
        title:   discount_popup_title,
        body:    discount_popup_body,
        class:   'sheet--discount-popup'
    } %}

    {#
      The script's whole configuration, on one element it can find, rather than
      five `theme.settings.get()` calls duplicated into an inline `<script>`.

      `data-signature` is the T-3.03 mechanism: it is hashed in JS into the
      storage key, so **changing the offer shows the popup again to everyone who
      dismissed the old one.** A fixed key would silently withhold a new offer
      from every visitor who ever saw the previous one.
    #}
    <div data-discount-popup
         hidden
         data-delay="{{ theme.settings.get('discount_popup_delay', 5) }}"
         data-once="{{ theme.settings.get('discount_popup_once', true) ? '1' : '0' }}"
         data-signature="{{ discount_popup_title }}|{{ discount_popup_text }}|{{ discount_popup_code }}"></div>
{% endif %}
